On MongoDB 7.0-style vector support you typically see indexes like HNSW, IVF or DiskANN. A representative create-index command (Mongo shell syntax) is:
db.profiles.createIndex(
  { embedding: "vector" },
  { vector: { dimensions: 1536, method: "hnsw", metric: "cosine", M: 16, efConstruction: 200 } }
)
(Exact option names vary by implementation; Cosmos-managed vector features may expose vendor-specific options but the above is the MongoDB 7.0-style vector index shape.)
